# Officious Interrogation counts the creatures only of the target players still legal as it resolves (CR 608.2b; its ruling: "Any
# target players that are no longer legal targets by the time Officious Interrogation resolves won't have their creatures counted").
# Bot1 targets itself and Bot2. In response Bot2, with High Fae Trickster letting it cast spells as though they had flash, casts
# Leyline of Sanctity ("You have hexproof"), so Bot2 is no longer a legal target: its Trickster is not counted, and Bot1, still a
# legal target, investigates once for its own Memnite.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Plains
Island
Memnite
Officious Interrogation
Plains
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
